Hi Claire,

Thanks for the very useful feedback -- we'll use this to provide clearer instructions on setting up the toolchain on Mac to support compiling packages from source.

I'm using a dev build of RRO 8.0.3 (based on R 3.1.3) -- I have Xcode and gfortran installed -- and I was able to install devtools, httr and bitpos just fine. Having done do, I was able to compile and install rstan just fine using the following commands:

library(checkpoint)
checkpoint("2015-04-10")
library(devtools)
library(httr)
library(bitops)
source('http://mc-stan.org/rstan/install.R')
install_rstan()
library(rstan)

I was however unable to compile wesleyburr's tsinterp package. The linker came back with the error "library not found for -lquadmath" (I've included the full output below). It's not clear to me though if this is simply a problem with the tsinterp package. Has anyone had success compiling this package on Yosemite?

# David Smith

