Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rropen/c/vkmiSiHd-C0/m/-NUAFbJ3NPEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Qingyun,

On Windows and Linux, to enable the MKL and install the Revobase package you will also need to download and install the "MKL Math Library" installer from the downloads page <http://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/download/#download>. You can find more info in the installation instructions <http://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/documents/rro/installation/>.

There is no separate installer on Mac because multi-threading is provided by the native Accelerate Framework. There's also no separate Revobase package for Mac -- it's not required as the Accelerate Framework sets the number of threads automatically.

Cheers,
# David Smith

